# Bootstrap questionnaire — {{ project_name }}

Every decision this project must make before its standards are binding. It works with any AI
tool or with none: answer in `.baseline/answers.yaml` (same ids), then apply the answers to the
documents named in **Writes to**.

How to answer each question: `default`, a value, or `later`. `later` is always allowed. The
question is then recorded in `docs/DECISION-QUEUE.md` and is never guessed.

Questions are asked **one phase at a time**, numbered, with the recommended default and its
trade-off. A phase is finished when every question in it is answered or deferred.

The rows below are the **headline** questions. Every document also has a `## Parameters` table;
its remaining open parameters are offered in the same phase as one bulk list — "accept all
defaults, or name the ones to change". `node scripts/params.mjs <path>` prints that list for the
documents a phase writes to.

---

## Phase 0 — Intake

| Id | Question | Default | Writes to |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| 0.1 | In two or three sentences: what does the product do, for whom, and what does it deliberately not do? | {{ project_description or '— (required)' }} | `AGENTS.md` |
| 0.2 | Who decides on standards and ADRs (names or handles)? | {{ owner }} | frontmatter `owner`, ADR `deciders` |
| 0.3 | Is anything already in production? | no | `docs/04-adr/README.md` governance mode |
| 0.4 | ADR governance mode: `pre-production` (amend in place until first production deploy) or `immutable`? | `pre-production` if 0.3 is no, else `immutable` | `docs/04-adr/README.md` |

